<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows $596 mln June 25.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows $596 mln June 25.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $596 million surplus on June 25 in the commercial forex market, according to the central bank.</p>
<p>The central bank issued the following breakdown:</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 25</p>
<p>Exports: $241.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $259.7 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $920 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $305.5 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $596 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.985 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $4.794 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $7.777 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $6.412 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $556 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
